  "title": "SignRR and SeMoCo: Motion and Language Fusion Frameworks",
  "summary": "SignRR proposes a retrieve-and-refine paradigm for sign language production, combining real motion retrieval with learned refinement to achieve coherent signing sequences. SeMoCo introduces a semantic-first motion codec with dual-axis motion generation, enabling efficient motion tokenization and language conditioning for motion generation.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "SignRR integrates real motion retrieval with a Residual VQ-VAE framework for coherent signing sequences.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "SeMoCo uses a dual-axis motion generator to encode both semantic and kinematic information in motion tokens.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Both frameworks achieve state-of-the-art performance in motion generation with strong text-to-motion results.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
